  "description": "Fuaran.Compute.LinearAlgebra — a small, dense, column-major linear-algebra contract whose every operation runs in one pinned floating-point order, so its answers are byte-identical on .NET, under Fable and in every host that ports it: an opaque immutable Matrix, vectors as Fuaran.Core's Vector<float> (a float column is an input without a copy), the level-1 operations (dot, axpy, scale, add, sub and the scaled norm2), gemv in column-axpy order, gemm in per-element k order, the Gram matrix, triangular solves over a checked UpperTriangular, the one Givens rotation, least squares by a streaming Givens QR whose O(p²) state survives a restart through its wire codec, batch and pivoted Householder factorizations, the pinned elementary functions exp, ln, log10 and float-exponent pow behind one special-value table, Poisson and Gamma log-link generalised linear models by IRLS with the same bits and iteration count on every host, typed errors and canonical NaN out. No fused multiply-add and no host mathematics call on any host. Fable-clean.",
